From: billyli19
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: PCIe sleep floor at CX retention

Same change as the SM8650 one (kernel-sm8650 0047). The suspend OPP keeps
PCIe's DDR vote in the sleep set so the system can resume, but it also
required CX at low_svs, and a CX level above retention for the whole sleep
rules out CX collapse. On an AYN Odin 3 cxsd, aosd and ddr stayed at 0
through every s2idle (sleep-stats, 2026-11-11) and the battery fell about
2.5 % an hour asleep.

Keep the DDR vote and ask only for CX retention.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index ea579305c..2bf87ae21 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -5702,11 +5702,13 @@ opp-16000000 {
 
 				/*
 				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
-				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it.
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it. DDR stays
+				 * voted so the system can resume, CX only at retention so
+				 * it can still collapse.
 				 */
 				opp-suspend-1 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
-					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_ret>;
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
 					opp-suspend;
 				};
